## Scope and constraints

Continue the Phase 18 Java 5.5.1 parity work from the current repository state. Keep the Java oracle read-only; do not start Docker or contact a Broker, and do not push, tag, publish, or deploy. Keep implementation and documentation changes in separate commits.

## Actions and evidence

- Confirmed the current code revision was `c3842532` and the worktree contained only an unfinished compatibility-map documentation edit.
- Implemented `WriteLongAsString` in the shared Protocol JSON writers. Mapped Java long-valued bean properties and offset-table values to JSON strings; quoted numeric keys in route `brokerAddrs` while preserving numeric `currIdMap` keys.
- Added fixture-backed assertions across inherited body, route, and heartbeat serialization cases, including the existing Java expected outputs for populated DTOs.
- Committed implementation as `de2d1a8f feat(protocol): support long writer feature`.
- `TZ=UTC cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --all-features --locked`: passed, 122 unit tests, all Protocol integration targets, and 42 doctests.
- `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`: passed.
- `TZ=UTC mvn -o -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify`: passed, including all 37 scenarios and Java/Rust cross-decodes.
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check`: passed.
- Updated the compatibility API/config map and release checklist for `WriteNonStringKeyAsString` and `WriteLongAsString`; corrected the stale 9/48 and 39-unmapped inventory to 11/48 and 37-unmapped.

